    "text": "# Investigation note: metric M384271, reporting month 2026-10-31\n\n**1. Executive finding**\nM384271 is in the **Red (needs attention)** provisional band. Its provisional rate is **62.5% (10 of 16)**, above the 60% red threshold you gave. That is 6.25 points lower than September, but still red. The rate has been in the red band in 7 of the last 8 months.\n\n**2. Current status and period (2026-10-31)**\n- 24 metric rows, one per application, so 24 applications.\n- Compliant: 10 rows. Non_Compliant: 6. Pending: 3. Not_Applicable: 5.\n- Denominator: 16 rows, which are all Compliant and Non_Compliant rows. Pending and Not_Applicable rows are left out, which matches the inferred EXCLUDES_PENDING scope.\n- Numerator: 10 rows. In this month every numerator row is a **Compliant** row.\n\n**3. Movement against the prior month**\n- The provisional rate went from 68.75% (11/16) in September to 62.5% (10/16) in October, a change of −6.25 points (provisional).\n- The denominator stayed at 16, so the change comes from one fewer numerator row.\n- Over 12 months the rate rose from about 38–45% (Nov 2025–Jan 2026) to 59–71% (May–Oct 2026).\n- Rows in scope grew from 16 to 24 over the year, so part of the change may come from which applications reported. I have not run a breakdown of continuing versus new applications.\n**4. Main contributors (the 6 Non_Compliant rows)**\n- **Super division:** Super_Division_02 has 2 of 6, Super_Division_04 has 2, Super_Division_05 has 1 and Super_Division_07 has 1. The other four super divisions have none.\n- **Legal entity:** only Legal_Entity_05 appears twice (Application_01419 and Application_00032). Every other legal entity appears once at most.\n- **Applications:** Application_00351, 00896, 01419, 00368, 01095 and 00032.\n**5. Testing and exception observations**\n- 13 rows have a completed test: 9 passed and 4 failed. All 4 failed rows are Non_Compliant. Their reasons are Test_Failed (1), Remediation_Overdue (1) and Open_Findings_Outstanding (2).\n- The other 2 Non_Compliant rows have a test still pending, with the reason Test_Overdue.\n- 2 rows are Exempt:\n  - one is Compliant (Exemption_Conditions_Met) and counts in the denominator;\n  - one is Not_Applicable (Exemption_Approved) and does not count.\n- The 3 Pending rows are Test_Scheduled or Test_In_Progress and do not count in the denominator.\n\n**6. Areas for further investigation (these are hypotheses, not findings)**\n- **Check which way the rate should be read.** This needs confirming before acting on the band. You defined a higher rate as worse, but in the data the numerator is made up of Compliant rows. Read that way, a 62.5% rate would mean 10 of 16 rows are compliant.\n- Whether the 2 overdue tests and 2 outstanding findings rows have remediation in progress. The data does not show this.\n- Whether the 3 Pending rows will move the rate once they are resolved and enter the denominator.\n- How much of the rise from early 2026 comes from new applications starting to report rather than changes in existing ones.\n\n**7. Limitations of the evidence**\n- The rate, the band thresholds, the denominator scope and what the numerator means are all provisional. None of them is confirmed by the client.\n- The populations are small (16 in the denominator), so one row moves the rate by about 6 points.\n- The dataset has no metric names, causes, owners or remediation status. Nothing here should be read as a cause or as completed remediation.\n- All names in the dataset are synthetic.",
